{
  "raw": {
    "https://wp.newemployees.hr.uconn.edu/": {
      "title": "UConn Cookie Information",
      "description": "UConn Careers | UConn Careers | University of Connecticut Skip to Navigation Skip to UConn Search Skip to Content Our websites may use cookies to personalize and enhance your experience. By continuing without changing your cookie settings, you agree to this collection. For more information, please see our University Websites Privacy Notice . UConn Cookie Information What are Cookies? Authentication Cookies Analytics Cookies Opt Out Web cookies (also called HTTP cookies , browser cookies , or simply cookies ) are small pieces of data that websites store on your device (computer, phone, etc.) through your web browser. They are used to remember information about you and your interactions with the site. Purpose of Cookies: Session Management : Keeping you logged in Remembering items in a shopping cart Saving language or theme preferences Personalization : Tailoring content or ads based on your previous activity Tracking & Analytics : Monitoring browsing behavior for analytics or marketing purposes Types of Cookies: Session Cookies : Temporary; deleted when you close your browser Used for things like keeping you logged in during a single session Persistent Cookies : Stored on your device until they expire or are manually deleted Used for remembering login credentials, settings, etc. First-Party Cookies : Set by the website you're visiting directly Third-Party Cookies : Set by other domains (usually advertisers) embedded in the website Commonly used for tracking across multiple sites Authentication cookies are a special type of web cookie used to identify and verify a user after they log in to a website or web application. What They Do: Once you log in to a site, the server creates an authentication cookie and sends it to your browser. This cookie: Proves to the website that you're logged in Prevents you from having to log in again on every page you visit Can persist across sessions if you select \"Remember me\" What's Inside an Authentication Cookie? Typically, it contains: A unique session ID (not your actual password) Optional metadata (e.g., expiration time, security flags) Analytics cookies are cookies used to collect data about how visitors interact with a website . Their primary purpose is to help website owners understand and improve user experience by analyzing things like: How users navigate the site Which pages are most/least visited How long users stay on each page What device, browser, or location the user is from What They Track: Some examples of data analytics cookies may collect: Page views and time spent on pages Click paths (how users move from page to page) Bounce rate (users who leave without interacting) User demographics (location, language, device) Referring websites (how users arrived at the site) Here’s how you can disable cookies in common browsers: 1. Google Chrome Open Chrome and click the three vertical dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies and other site data . Choose your preferred option: Block all cookies (not recommended, can break most websites). Block third-party cookies (can block ads and tracking cookies). 2. Mozilla Firefox Open Firefox and click the three horizontal lines in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy & Security . Under the Enhanced Tracking Protection section, choose Strict to block most cookies or Custom to manually choose which cookies to block. 3. Safari Open Safari and click Safari in the top-left corner of the screen. Go to Preferences > Privacy . Check Block all cookies to stop all cookies, or select options to block third-party cookies. 4. Microsoft Edge Open Edge and click the three horizontal dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy, search, and services > Cookies and site permissions . Select your cookie settings from there, including blocking all cookies or blocking third-party cookies. 5. On Mobile (iOS/Android) For Safari on iOS: Go to Settings > Safari > Privacy & Security > Block All Cookies . For Chrome on Android: Open the app, tap the three dots, go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies . Be Aware: Disabling cookies can make your online experience more difficult. Some websites may not load properly, or you may be logged out frequently. Also, certain features may not work as expected. UConn University of Connecticut Search University of Connecticut Search UConn A to Z Index UConn A to Z Index Site A-Z UConn A-Z UConn Careers Search this Site Search in https://wp.newemployees.hr.uconn.edu/> Search UConn Careers {css}{javascript}{form} Apply for Jobs Applicant Login Career Portal Help Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine Your Search {search-keyword} Filter Results {search-filters button-text=\"Filter Results\"} {messages} {pages} {/form} © University of Connecticut Disclaimers, Privacy & Copyright Accessibility Webmaster Login"
    },
    "https://careers.pageuppeople.com/967/cw/en-us/listing/": {
      "title": "UConn Cookie Information",
      "description": "UConn Careers | UConn Careers | University of Connecticut Skip to Navigation Skip to UConn Search Skip to Content Our websites may use cookies to personalize and enhance your experience. By continuing without changing your cookie settings, you agree to this collection. For more information, please see our University Websites Privacy Notice . UConn Cookie Information What are Cookies? Authentication Cookies Analytics Cookies Opt Out Web cookies (also called HTTP cookies , browser cookies , or simply cookies ) are small pieces of data that websites store on your device (computer, phone, etc.) through your web browser. They are used to remember information about you and your interactions with the site. Purpose of Cookies: Session Management : Keeping you logged in Remembering items in a shopping cart Saving language or theme preferences Personalization : Tailoring content or ads based on your previous activity Tracking & Analytics : Monitoring browsing behavior for analytics or marketing purposes Types of Cookies: Session Cookies : Temporary; deleted when you close your browser Used for things like keeping you logged in during a single session Persistent Cookies : Stored on your device until they expire or are manually deleted Used for remembering login credentials, settings, etc. First-Party Cookies : Set by the website you're visiting directly Third-Party Cookies : Set by other domains (usually advertisers) embedded in the website Commonly used for tracking across multiple sites Authentication cookies are a special type of web cookie used to identify and verify a user after they log in to a website or web application. What They Do: Once you log in to a site, the server creates an authentication cookie and sends it to your browser. This cookie: Proves to the website that you're logged in Prevents you from having to log in again on every page you visit Can persist across sessions if you select \"Remember me\" What's Inside an Authentication Cookie? Typically, it contains: A unique session ID (not your actual password) Optional metadata (e.g., expiration time, security flags) Analytics cookies are cookies used to collect data about how visitors interact with a website . Their primary purpose is to help website owners understand and improve user experience by analyzing things like: How users navigate the site Which pages are most/least visited How long users stay on each page What device, browser, or location the user is from What They Track: Some examples of data analytics cookies may collect: Page views and time spent on pages Click paths (how users move from page to page) Bounce rate (users who leave without interacting) User demographics (location, language, device) Referring websites (how users arrived at the site) Here’s how you can disable cookies in common browsers: 1. Google Chrome Open Chrome and click the three vertical dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies and other site data . Choose your preferred option: Block all cookies (not recommended, can break most websites). Block third-party cookies (can block ads and tracking cookies). 2. Mozilla Firefox Open Firefox and click the three horizontal lines in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy & Security . Under the Enhanced Tracking Protection section, choose Strict to block most cookies or Custom to manually choose which cookies to block. 3. Safari Open Safari and click Safari in the top-left corner of the screen. Go to Preferences > Privacy . Check Block all cookies to stop all cookies, or select options to block third-party cookies. 4. Microsoft Edge Open Edge and click the three horizontal dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy, search, and services > Cookies and site permissions . Select your cookie settings from there, including blocking all cookies or blocking third-party cookies. 5. On Mobile (iOS/Android) For Safari on iOS: Go to Settings > Safari > Privacy & Security > Block All Cookies . For Chrome on Android: Open the app, tap the three dots, go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies . Be Aware: Disabling cookies can make your online experience more difficult. Some websites may not load properly, or you may be logged out frequently. Also, certain features may not work as expected. UConn University of Connecticut Search University of Connecticut Search UConn A to Z Index UConn A to Z Index Site A-Z UConn A-Z UConn Careers Search this Site Search in https://wp.newemployees.hr.uconn.edu/> Search UConn Careers Apply for Jobs Applicant Login Career Portal Help Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine Your Search Filter Results Work type Full-time 71 Locations Middlesex County Extension Ctr 1 Other - please see posting for additional information 4 School of Law 3 School of Social Work 1 UConn Avery Point 1 UConn Hartford 3 UConn Health (Farmington) 4 UConn Stamford 5 UConn Storrs 49 UConn Waterbury 1 Categories Academic Programs and Services 2 Administrative Services 7 Athletics (Coaches, Trainers, Specialists) 1 Audit and Compliance 3 Custodial 2 Dining Services 1 Executive 2 Facilities 4 Faculty Department Head/Director 2 Faculty Extension Educator 2 Faculty Non Tenure Track 7 Faculty Temporary 1 Faculty Tenure Track 5 Fiscal, Accounting and Budget 4 Grants and Contracts 2 Information Technology 9 Maintenance and Trades 4 Postdoctoral Research Associates 3 Public Safety 4 Research 5 Student Programs and Services 9 Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Department Search # Location Closes Pre-Award Specialist - Faculty Shared Services SPS Faculty Shared Services (SPS Preaward) 499342 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR) is recruiting talented grants and contracts/sponsored project professionals to join our research administration team. The Pre-Award Grants and Contracts Specialists provide day to day management and oversight for a high volume of pre-award administration. Director of Research Technology Services ITS Research IT 499682 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 Under the general direction of the Chief Information Officer, provides executive, technical, and operational leadership for technology services supporting the University’s research enterprise within Information Technology Services (ITS). The Director is responsible for developing and implementing solutions, policies, and services that advance the University’s research mission through effective use of technology. The Director serves as the primary liaison between ITS, the Office of the Vice President for Research (OVPR), faculty researchers, research centers, and other stakeholders to ensure that technology services effectively support current and emerging research needs and has a dotted line reporting relationship to the Vice President for Research, Innovation and Entrepreneurship. IT Manager Network Engr and Design 499714 UConn Storrs Sep 18 2026 The University of Connecticut Information Technology Services (ITS) is seeking a Manager of Network Engineering and Operations to lead the University's Network Engineering and Network Operations teams. This position is responsible for overseeing the daily operation, support, and continuous improvement of the University's enterprise network infrastructure and services that support the academic, research, administrative, and residential communities across the Storrs campus, regional campuses, and the School of Law. Student Employment Manager UConn Recreation 499802 UConn Storrs Sep 17 2026 UConn Recreation is seeking a motivated and detail-oriented professional to serve as our Student Employment Manager.  In this impactful role, the manager will help support the student employee experience by coordinating key human resources functions, including recruitment, onboarding, and payroll administration. Cash Operations Specialist Bursar 499826 UConn Storrs Sep 24 2026 The Cash Operations Specialist serves as the primary financial administrator in the Office of the Bursar for University deposits, responsible for daily reconciliation of incoming funds between the University’s bank accounts and the State and University general ledger systems. This position monitors departments’ compliance with State statutes for depositing and provides training assistance to University staff for depositing and cash handling. Assistant, Associate, or Full Professor - Addictions and Behavioral Health Focus Social Work Instruct and Rsrch 499822 School of Social Work The University of Connecticut School of Social Work is pleased to invite applications for a full-time (9-month appointment), open-rank, tenure-line position.  We seek a highly motivated, productive, and collaborative scholar committed to advancing research and education in addictions and behavioral health. We welcome applicants with expertise in intervention research, particularly those developing, evaluating, and implementing technology-based interventions. Dining Services Assistant Manager Dining Services 499823 UConn Storrs Sep 16 2026 The Department of Dining Services at the University of Connecticut has an opening for an Assistant Area Manager. This position reports to the Manager 2 or an appropriate designee and assists in providing effective supervision and leadership within the Department of Dining Services. Postdoctoral Research Associate Statistics 499493 UConn Storrs Oct 23 2026 The Department of Statistics at the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences, University of Connecticut (UConn), invites applications for a full-time Postdoctoral Research Associate position. The successful candidate will engage in innovative research addressing statistical methodology, machine learning, and/or learning techniques in complex biomedical and health-related challenges. We particularly focus on real-world applications in psychology, psychiatry, mental health, aging, and related fields. Senior Public Policy Analyst Innovations Institute 499803 Other - please see posting for additional information The University of Connecticut School of Social Work seeks qualified applicants to be hired as a Senior Public Policy Analyst (Research Associate I), to be part of the Innovations Institute at the University of Connecticut’s School of Social Work. \n\nThe position will be part of the School of Social Work’s growing portfolio of public policy, technical assistance, financing, and evaluation activities in partnership with local, state, and federal government agencies and organizations on behalf of children, youth, and families. Positions with Innovations Institute are fully remote, with expected travel to UConn’s Hartford Campus twice annually. Innovations Institute will be hiring up to two (2) candidates. Quantum CT Evaluation Project Manager Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499814 UConn Storrs Sep 28 2026 The NSF Quantum Technologies Engine in Connecticut (QuantumCT Engine), led by the University of Connecticut, aims to advance American quantum innovation and secure the domestic quantum supply chain by accelerating the commercialization of quantum technologies for national defense, biotechnology, and financial services. Through innovation, applied research leading to new technologies, support for inventors and entrepreneurs and workforce development, the QuantumCT Engine will advance quantum sensing, secured communications, computing, and materials through shared test bed, deep-tech incubator, and translation pathways.\n\nThe Evaluation Project Manager will be responsible for assisting with day-to-day operations of all evaluation-related activities. They will also help manage evaluation meeting logistics and facilitation, implementation, data management and analyses, supervision of undergraduate and graduate students, and evaluation dissemination and use activities. Job responsibilities cluster into five categories: project management and coordination, evaluation design, evaluation implementation and data analysis, reporting, and quality assurance. The Evaluation Project Manager will report to Dr. Bianca Montrosse-Moorhead, incoming Department Head and Professor in the Department of Educational Psychology, and QuantumCT Engine External Evaluation Lead. Assistant Professor, Public/Nonprofit Management Public Policy 499820 UConn Hartford The School of Public Policy (SPP) at the University of Connecticut (UConn) seeks to fill a tenure track position at the rank of Assistant Professor starting in August 2027. IT-SLE Operations Analyst IT Student Life and Enrollment 499834 UConn Storrs Sep 15 2026 UConn Student Life and Enrollment is seeking applicants for its IT-SLE Operations Analyst position.  This position serves as a bridge between business intelligence, data analysis, advanced analytics, and innovative AI solutions, incorporating AI into daily analytical processes and decision-making for operational teams. Assistant Director of Athletic Events & Facilities Athletics 499835 UConn Storrs Sep 14 2026 The University of Connecticut is accepting applications and nominations for a full-time position of Assistant Director of Athletic Events and Facilities. This individual will report directly to the Assistant Athletic Director for Events and Facilities and will assist in the planning, preparation, and execution of home athletic and special event operations. CEN Administrative Assistant CT Education Network ASC 499813 UConn Hartford Sep 11 2026 Under the direction of the Executive Director, the Administrative Assistant serves as a key member of the Connecticut Education Network (CEN) team, helping keep the organization running smoothly, efficiently, and on track. This role is often the hub that connects people, projects, and priorities across CEN, coordinating administrative processes, managing schedules, preparing reports, tracking operational activities, supporting member engagement, and identifying opportunities to streamline workflows and improve efficiency. Quantum CT Technical Operating Manager Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499816 UConn Health (Farmington) Sep 18 2026 The NSF Quantum Technologies Engine in Connecticut (QuantumCT Engine), led by the University of Connecticut, aims to advance American quantum innovation and secure the domestic quantum supply chain by accelerating the commercialization of quantum technologies for national defense, biotechnology, and financial services. Through innovation, applied research leading to new technologies, support for inventors and entrepreneurs and workforce development, the QuantumCT Engine will advance quantum sensing, secured communications, computing, and materials through shared test bed, deep-tech incubator, and translation pathways.\n\nReporting to the Director of Technology Incubation & Venture Development in Technology Commercialization Services, this position will oversee and support the operational and technical management of the quantum technology incubator. This includes overseeing the day-to-day technical operations, maintaining specialized infrastructure, and serving as a resource for startups, helping them navigate facility use, equipment training, and compliance with safety protocols. He/she will design protocols for lab and equipment usage, establish preventative maintenance schedules for mission-critical infrastructure, maintain compliance with relevant industry standards for quantum research environments, and be a liaison between Quantum CT startups and collaborators. Custodian Student Union 498966 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 The State of Connecticut, University of Connecticut’s Student Union and Event Services department has one custodial job opening at the Storrs Campus that is 3rd shift, 11:00 PM–7:00 AM, Wednesday–Sunday. Working under the supervision of the Lead Custodian, Supervising Custodian, or Building Services Manager, the successful candidate will be accountable for performing a full range of basic tasks in the cleaning and maintenance of the Student Union building. Senior Security Compliance Specialist Ntl Inst Undersea Vehicle Tech 499474 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The National Institute for Undersea Vehicle Technology (NIUVT) at the University of Connecticut seeks qualified applicants for a Senior Research Compliance Specialist (P5) position. Network Service Administrator 1 or 2 Telecommunications 499730 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 Under the supervision of a designated team leader, the Network Administrator 1/2 for Collaboration Services provides technical support for the planning, implementation, administration, monitoring, troubleshooting, and lifecycle management of the University's enterprise voice and collaboration services and supporting network infrastructure. The position supports the integration of voice and collaboration platforms with network, identity, telecommunications carrier, and other enterprise systems and participates in the evaluation and implementation of technology solutions. Incident Response Manager and Security Operations Team Lead Info Technology Security 499767 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 Under the direction of the Chief Information Security Officer, the Incident Response Manager & Security Operations Team Lead is responsible for leading the University's Security Operations and Incident Response functions in support of the University of Connecticut Information Security Office. Assistant or Associate Research Professor Innovations Institute 499772 Other - please see posting for additional information The University of Connecticut School of Social Work’s Innovations Institute invites applications for a full-time (11-month appointment) non-tenure-track assistant or associate research professor position. Positions with Innovations Institute are fully remote with expected travel to UConn’s Hartford Campus annually. This appointment does not lead to permanent academic tenure and must be renewed annually.\n\nThe selected candidates will serve as the co-Principal Investigator and Project Director for the evaluation of Connecticut’s Rural Health Transformation Project (RHTP). The selected candidate will apply knowledge, concepts, principles, and skills across Connecticut’s RHTP and ultimately support multiple research and evaluation projects or initiatives within the Innovations Institute. In addition, the successful candidate will bring expertise in implementation science and mixed-methods research, including the design, execution, and interpretation of quantitative and qualitative analyses. The candidate will contribute methodological expertise to complex health systems evaluations while developing an independent program of research and extramural funding aligned with the mission of the Innovations Institute and the School of Social Work. Financial Assistant 2 Fine Arts 499780 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The School of Fine Arts Financial Services Office seeks qualified applicants for a full-time position as Financial Assistant 2 within the Office of the Dean. Compliance Specialist Registrar 499798 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The Office of the Registrar at the University of Connecticut invites applications for a full-time, permanent Registrar Specialist (P3) position. Reporting to an Assistant Registrar, this role is responsible for managing multiple high-level, detail-oriented projects focused mainly on audit, compliance, and operational support while delivering exceptional customer service in a high-volume environment. The successful candidate will demonstrate the ability to work with accuracy, efficiency, and professionalism in a fast-paced and dynamic setting. Information Security Assessment and Analysis Team Lead Info Technology Security 499811 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 Under the general direction of the Chief Information Security Officer, the Information Security Assessment and Analysis Team Lead is responsible for leading the University's Security Assessment and Security Analysis programs in support of the University of Connecticut Information Security Office. Senior Internal Auditor (University Staff Professional 2) Audit and Mgmt Advisory Svcs 499510 UConn Storrs The Office of Audit and Management Advisory Services (AMAS) is seeking a Senior Internal Auditor (University Staff Professional 2) to conduct internal audits under the general direction of the Audit Director. The Senior Internal Auditor will support AMAS audit activities on the UConn and UConn Health campuses, with a primary work location in Storrs. Quantum CT Project Manager Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499815 UConn Health (Farmington), UConn Storrs Sep 18 2026 The NSF Quantum Technologies Engine in Connecticut (QuantumCT Engine), led by the University of Connecticut, aims to advance American quantum innovation and secure the domestic quantum supply chain by accelerating the commercialization of quantum technologies for national defense, biotechnology and financial services. Through innovation, applied research leading to new technologies, support for inventors and entrepreneurs and workforce development, the QuantumCT Engine will advance quantum sensing, secured communications, computing, and materials through shared test bed, deep-tech incubator, and translation pathways.\n\nReporting to the NSF Engine Project Manager and CEO, the Project Manager is responsible for coordinating and supporting the implementation of the QuantumCT NSF Engines initiative. The position manages project activities from initiation through completion, ensuring alignment with project goals, sponsor requirements, and organizational objectives. The Project Manager serves as a central point of coordination among UConn, Yale University, industry partners, researchers, and other stakeholders, facilitating communication, tracking deliverables, supporting strategic initiatives, and ensuring successful execution of project activities. Quantum CT Technology Transfer Licensing Associate Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499817 UConn Health (Farmington) Sep 18 2026 The NSF Quantum Technologies Engine in Connecticut (QuantumCT Engine), led by the University of Connecticut, aims to advance American quantum innovation and secure the domestic quantum supply chain by accelerating the commercialization of quantum technologies for national defense, biotechnology and financial services. Through innovation, applied research leading to new technologies, support for inventors and entrepreneurs and workforce development, the QuantumCT Engine will advance quantum sensing, secured communications, computing, and materials through shared test bed, deep-tech incubator, and translation pathways.\n\nReporting to the Senior Director of Licensing at the Technology Commercialization the Technology Transfer Licensing Associate Services, this position will work closely with the OVPR’s Technology Commercialization Services (TCS) technology office to evaluate and manage new inventions, licensing agreements, evaluate IP work with the patent council’s office, and lead discussions for transactions, filings, and contract negotiation.\n\nThe successful candidate will be energetic, accessible, responsive, and possess the ability to foster collaboration in a dynamic organizational culture to facilitate the translation of quantum science and research to market. Quantum CT Workforce Development Coordinator Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499818 UConn Storrs Sep 18 2026 The NSF Quantum Technologies Engine in Connecticut (QuantumCT Engine), led by the University of Connecticut, aims to advance American quantum innovation and secure the domestic quantum supply chain by accelerating the commercialization of quantum technologies for national defense, biotechnology and financial services. Through innovation, applied research leading to new technologies, support for inventors and entrepreneurs and workforce development, the QuantumCT Engine will advance quantum sensing, secured communications, computing, and materials through shared test bed, deep-tech incubator, and translation pathways.\n\nReporting to the CEO of QuantumCT, and working closely with the Workforce Pillar Leads, the Workforce Development Coordinator is responsible for supporting the development, implementation, and coordination of workforce development initiatives for the QuantumCT projects. This individual reports directly to the UConn Quantum NSF Enginge Workforce Lead and CEO.  Their overall function is to provide the Director with comprehensive operational, logistical, and administrative support.  Major responsibilities include communications and digital presence; event planning and execution; student recruitment, cohort coordination and student support; and tracking participation metrics and programmatic outcomes. Continuous Quality Improvement Manager (Research Scientist) Innovations Institute 499791 Other - please see posting for additional information Innovations Institute is seeking applicants for the Continuous Quality Improvement Manager (Research Scientist). The successful candidate will direct continuous quality improvement (CQI) efforts across Innovations’ disseminated practice models, including Wraparound, Mobile Response and Stabilization Services (MRSS), FOCUS, and PEARLS. The contribution will be measured in terms of CQI deliverables completed across contracted states and sites. Successful candidates will be expected to broaden participation among members of under-represented groups; demonstrate through research and/or community engagement the commitment to, and support of, diversity in the learning experience; and integrate multicultural experiences into CQI tools, reports, and conversations. Positions with Innovations Institute are fully remote with expected travel to UConn’s Hartford Campus twice annually at the employee's expense. Finance Manager CLAS Business Center (CLAS Shared Services) 499794 UConn Storrs Sep 15 2026 The College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Dean's Office seeks applicants for a full-time position as a Finance Manager 1 for the CLAS Shared Services Business Center. The Finance Manager serves as an advanced senior resource within the CLAS Shared Services Business Center and provides leadership, technical expertise, and supervision of staff.  This position is responsible for managing day-to-day operations, overseeing and delegating to assigned staff, and reviewing and analyzing the fiscal and administrative operations for the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. Clinical Instructor-Coordinator of Clinical Placements Nursing Instruct and Research 499795 UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut, Elisabeth DeLuca School of Nursing (SON) is seeking applications to fill a full-time, 10-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor -Coordinator of Clinical Placements position.  Under the direction of the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, the faculty member will serve as coordinator of clinical placement sites for pre-licensure nursing students, will supervise students and preceptors in clinical work, will engage in scholarly and professional service activities, and will teach six credits per academic year. Director of Engineering Student Engagement Engineering Undergrad Programs 499805 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The College of Engineering at the University of Connecticut seeks a full-time professional staff member to serve as Director of Engineering Student Engagement. This position provides strategic leadership for high-impact educational experiences that enhance undergraduate engineering student engagement, success, leadership development, and global learning. Academic Advisor 2 Engineering Undergrad Programs 499806 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The College of Engineering at the University of Connecticut is seeking a full-time, professional staff Academic Advisor 2 at the Storrs campus. Academic advising is mandatory for every student, every semester, and the timely monitoring of degree progress is critical for the College of Engineering’s ABET accreditation. Associate Director, CT Sentencing Commission Public Policy 499720 UConn Hartford Sep 10 2026 The Associate Director of the CT Sentencing Commission will work with the Executive Director to lead professional staff members from IMRP, assigned to support the Commission. The Connecticut Sentencing Commission was established under Connecticut General Statutes 54-300 to review the existing criminal sentencing structure in the state, propose changes, including revisions to existing statutes, new criminal legislation, and updates to existing and proposed sentencing policies and practices, and make recommendations to the Governor, the General Assembly, and relevant criminal justice agencies. UConn Creamery Manager (Dining Services Manager 1) Animal Science 499774 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The Department of Animal Sciences, a part of the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, at the University of Connecticut, seeks applicants for a full-time UConn Creamery Manager 1 (Dining Services Manager 1). The Creamery Manager will provide effective management of the UConn Creamery, overseeing the production of ice cream, cheese, and other dairy products manufactured for the UConn Dairy Bar and related retail operations. Licensing Director, Physical Sciences (University Staff Professional 1) Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499368 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 The Office of the Vice President for Research at the University of Connecticut is seeking an energetic and experienced scientific R&D professional to join our Technology Commercialization Services (TCS) which is the Technology Transfer Office.  Working as part of a technology-focused team within the TCS the Licensing Director, Physical Sciences will be responsible for managing the evaluation, patenting, marketing of technologies, and licensing of Physical Sciences and engineering portfolio of university inventions. This also includes providing leadership, strategic oversight, and guidance through supervision, training, and mentorship of the licensing team, and support to startup companies affiliated with the University.\nThe Licensing Director, Physical Sciences will be a senior member of the team reporting to the Senior Director of Licensing to set the strategic direction of the commercialization strategies for the University. He/she must be an energetic and experienced mid-career professional with an established record and experience, a solid deal sheet that demonstrates out-licensing deals done by the candidate, someone who is accessible, responsive, and fosters collaboration in a dynamic organizational culture to facilitate the translation of science and research to market. This position requires U.S. Citizenship due to access to Controlled Classified Information. Manager of Stamford Admissions and Recruitment Stamford Campus 499786 UConn Stamford Sep 18 2026 The UConn Stamford Campus seeks candidates for the position of Manager of Stamford Admissions and Recruitment (Senior Student Services Program Administrator). Reporting to the Campus Dean, the Manager of Stamford Admissions and Recruitment provides strategic leadership for undergraduate admissions, recruitment, and enrollment management initiatives for the Stamford campus. Executive Assistant, Governmental Relations (University Education Assistant 3) Government Relations 499804 UConn Storrs Sep 08 2026 The University of Connecticut’s Office of Governmental Relations is hiring an Executive Assistant in Storrs, CT. This position provides office management and administrative support services. This position requires meticulous attention to detail and the ability to manage multiple priorities and deadlines in a fast-paced environment. Upward Bound Program Director, Windham High School Ctr for Access Postsec Success 499799 UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut’s Center for Access and Postsecondary Success (CAPS) seeks applicants to serve as the Upward Bound Program Director (Senior Student Services Program Administrator) for the Windham High School program. Based out of the UConn Storrs Campus, the Program Director will be responsible for the management and day-to-day administration of college preparation programming for first-generation and/or low-income high school students at Windham High School.\n\nThe Program Director will hire, train, supervise, and evaluate professional, instructional, and student staff; manage the approved budget for the program; prepare institutional, state, and federal reports; coordinate programming with campus units and community organizations; and evaluate program effectiveness. The Program Director will also serve as a resource to students, staff, parents, and other stakeholders on matters relating to college access, educational equity, student engagement, and postsecondary success. Upward Bound Program Director, Rockville High School Ctr for Access Postsec Success 499801 UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut’s Center for Access and Postsecondary Success (CAPS) seeks applicants to serve as the Upward Bound Math and Science Program Director (Senior Student Services Program Administrator) for the Rockville High School program. Based out of the Storrs Campus, the Program Director will be responsible for the management and day-to-day administration of college preparation programming for first-generation and low-income high school students interested in STEM at Rockville High School.\n\nThe Program Director will hire, train, supervise, and evaluate professional, instructional, and student staff; manage the approved budget for the program; prepare institutional, state, and federal reports; coordinate programming with campus units and community organizations; and evaluate program effectiveness. The Program Director will also serve as a resource to students, staff, parents, and other stakeholders on matters relating to college access, educational equity, student engagement, and postsecondary success. Instructor in Residence - UConn Waterbury Chemistry 499753 UConn Waterbury The Chemistry Department within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) at the University of Connecticut, Waterbury, invites applications for an Instructor in Residence (IiR) position. The successful candidate will primarily be responsible for teaching general and organic chemistry laboratory sections, as well as biochemistry laboratories in collaboration with other full-time faculty members. Accounts Payable and Automation Support Specialist P2 Accounts Payable 499590 UConn Storrs Sep 13 2026 The Accounts Payable and Automation Support Specialist administers, reconciles, audits and processes all transactions described within University Policies, Travel policy, and other related University policies, facilitates the workflow and processing of administrative paperwork and financial transactions, and assists with special projects as assigned. This position assists in the creation and implementation of departmental system applications and tools; provides day-to-day troubleshooting support, works with senior members to make process and workflow improvements and provides input to the decision-making process regarding procedures and process improvement initiatives. Professor and Department Head Social and Critical Inquiry 499673 UConn Storrs Oct 16 2026 The University of Connecticut seeks a dynamic leader to serve as Head of the Department of Social and Critical Inquiry (SCI). Web Application Developer Institutional Innovation 499768 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 Institutional Insights & Innovation (i3) is a small, agile digital enablement group embedded within the academic and research context at UConn. i3 is seeking an experienced Web Application Developer (Software Developer 2) to help design, build, deploy, and support a growing portfolio of institutional applications and digital platforms. This position is ideal for a versatile, experienced developer who enjoys working across the full lifecycle of a software product: understanding a problem, designing a solution, writing application code, integrating systems and data, deploying applications, troubleshooting production environments, and continually improving the systems they support. UConn SHaW Medical Office Coordinator - Avery Point Student Health and Wellness 499787 UConn Avery Point UConn Student Health and Wellness (SHaW) is hiring a Medical Office Coordinator (Business Operations Specialist 1) for our UConn Avery Point Campus. This is an in-person, permanent, 9-month (mid-August to mid-May) 35-hour-a-week position, responsible for front office and medical office operations to ensure positive student flow and student experience. One Stop Student Success Specialist One Stop Student Services 499762 UConn Storrs One Stop Student Services is seeking a dynamic, positive, and motivated professional to join our team! The Student Success Specialist (Student Services Program Assistant 2) position is primarily focused on providing exemplary customer service in a high-traffic public area while participating in several high-level, detailed projects concerning financial aid, admission, and registrar functions. A high degree of accuracy and efficiency while working in a fast-paced, dynamic environment is required. The successful candidate should expect to spend approximately 80% of their time on phone calls and emails with students and families. The current vacancy will work under the supervision of our One Stop Assistant Director for Financial Aid. Assistant, Associate, or Clinical Professor Psychological Sciences 499731 UConn Storrs Oct 05 2026 The Department of Psychological Sciences at the University of Connecticut in Storrs invites applications for the position of Clinical Professor (open rank)/Director of the Psychological Services Clinic to begin January 1st, 2027. This is a ten-month, non-tenure track, renewable position. The Psychological Services Clinic (PSC) is a training clinic in the Clinical Psychology Program through which Ph.D. students provide assessment and treatment services to children and adults under the supervision of licensed psychologists who are members of the clinical faculty. This position includes teaching graduate courses covering APA-required content (e.g., History and Systems) or clinical (e.g., Didactics & Practicum in Supervision) skills. In addition, the successful candidate will provide supervision of psychological assessments completed by graduate students within the PSC, provide assessment services and consultation to schools and community groups alongside graduate student trainees, and contribute to the supervision of child and adult therapy services provided by graduate students in the PSC. In conjunction with the clinic administrator, the candidate will also oversee PSC operations. Open Rank Clinical Professor - Legal Practice Program Law Instruction and Research 499734 School of Law The University of Connecticut (UConn) School of Law seeks candidates for an open-rank clinical faculty position in its Legal Practice Program (“LP Program”), beginning in the fall of 2027. Appointment may be made at the rank of Assistant, Associate, or Full Clinical Professor of Law, commensurate with the successful candidate’s qualifications and experience. The LP Program at UConn School of Law is an integrated seven-credit first-year program that provides experiential training in legal writing, legal research, oral advocacy, interviewing, counseling, negotiation, and professional identity formation. Open Rank Clinical Professor of Law/Director of Academic Success and Bar Prep Law Instruction and Research 499737 School of Law The University of Connecticut (UConn) School of Law seeks candidates for an open-rank clinical faculty position as Director of Academic Success and Bar Preparation beginning in the fall of 2027. This is a long-term contract faculty position within the Law School’s Professional Skills Faculty. Appointment may be made at the Assistant, Associate, or Full rank level, depending on qualifications and experience. Thomas F Gallivan Chair of Property Law Law Instruction and Research 499733 School of Law The University of Connecticut (UConn) School of Law seeks applications from lateral candidates for the Thomas F. Gallivan, Jr. Chair of Real Property Law. This is a tenured faculty position reserved for an outstanding scholar with an international or national reputation for excellence in property law scholarship, teaching, and service. Candidates for the Gallivan Chair should have an ambitious research agenda that seeks to shape contemporary conversations in property, land use and/or real estate law. We welcome applications from candidates pursuing innovative work within these areas that involves issues such as housing, local government, environmental law, and resiliency. Postdoctoral Research Associate Physiology and Neurobiology 499663 UConn Storrs The Sciolino Lab in the Department of Physiology and Neurobiology in the College of Liberal Arts & Sciences at the University of Connecticut on the Storrs Campus is seeking an exceptional Postdoctoral Research Associate to lead independent and collaborative projects in behavioral and systems neuroscience. The successful candidate will join an NIH-funded project investigating how neuromodulatory systems interact with central taste processing regions to regulate behavior.\n\nThis position is ideal for candidates interested in pursuing academic independence and developing expertise in neuromodulatory circuits, sensory processing, in vivo imaging, and/or behavior. Training and mentorship will be provided to support the development of independent fellowship and grant applications. More Jobs 21 Current opportunities Position Department Search # Location Closes Pre-Award 