t of, diversity in the learning experience; and integrate multicultural experiences into CQI tools, reports, and conversations. Positions with Innovations Institute are fully remote with expected travel to UConn’s Hartford Campus twice annually at the employee's expense. Finance Manager CLAS Business Center (CLAS Shared Services) 499794 UConn Storrs Sep 15 2026 The College of Liberal Arts & Sciences Dean's Office seeks applicants for a full-time position as a Finance Manager 1 for the CLAS Shared Services Business Center. The Finance Manager serves as an advanced senior resource within the CLAS Shared Services Business Center and provides leadership, technical expertise, and supervision of staff.  This position is responsible for managing day-to-day operations, overseeing and delegating to assigned staff, and reviewing and analyzing the fiscal and administrative operations for the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences. Clinical Instructor-Coordinator of Clinical Placements Nursing Instruct and Research 499795 UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut, Elisabeth DeLuca School of Nursing (SON) is seeking applications to fill a full-time, 10-month, non-tenure track Clinical Instructor -Coordinator of Clinical Placements position.  Under the direction of the Associate Dean for Academic Affairs, the faculty member will serve as coordinator of clinical placement sites for pre-licensure nursing students, will supervise students and preceptors in clinical work, will engage in scholarly and professional service activities, and will teach six credits per academic year. Director of Engineering Student Engagement Engineering Undergrad Programs 499805 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The College of Engineering at the University of Connecticut seeks a full-time professional staff member to serve as Director of Engineering Student Engagement. This position provides strategic leadership for high-impact educational experiences that enhance undergraduate engineering student engagement, success, leadership development, and global learning. Academic Advisor 2 Engineering Undergrad Programs 499806 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The College of Engineering at the University of Connecticut is seeking a full-time, professional staff Academic Advisor 2 at the Storrs campus. Academic advising is mandatory for every student, every semester, and the timely monitoring of degree progress is critical for the College of Engineering’s ABET accreditation. Associate Director, CT Sentencing Commission Public Policy 499720 UConn Hartford Sep 10 2026 The Associate Director of the CT Sentencing Commission will work with the Executive Director to lead professional staff members from IMRP, assigned to support the Commission. The Connecticut Sentencing Commission was established under Connecticut General Statutes 54-300 to review the existing criminal sentencing structure in the state, propose changes, including revisions to existing statutes, new criminal legislation, and updates to existing and proposed sentencing policies and practices, and make recommendations to the Governor, the General Assembly, and relevant criminal justice agencies. UConn Creamery Manager (Dining Services Manager 1) Animal Science 499774 UConn Storrs Sep 25 2026 The Department of Animal Sciences, a part of the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, at the University of Connecticut, seeks applicants for a full-time UConn Creamery Manager 1 (Dining Services Manager 1). The Creamery Manager will provide effective management of the UConn Creamery, overseeing the production of ice cream, cheese, and other dairy products manufactured for the UConn Dairy Bar and related retail operations. Licensing Director, Physical Sciences (University Staff Professional 1) Tech Comm and Industry Rltns (Vice President for Research) 499368 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 The Office of the Vice President for Research at the University of Connecticut is seeking an energetic and experienced scientific R&D professional to join our Technology Commercialization Services (TCS) which is the Technology Transfer Office.  Working as part of a technology-focused team within the TCS the Licensing Director, Physical Sciences will be responsible for managing the evaluation, patenting, marketing of technologies, and licensing of Physical Sciences and engineering portfolio of university inventions. This also includes providing leadership, strategic oversight, and guidance through supervision, training, and mentorship of the licensing team, and support to startup companies affiliated with the University.\nThe Licensing Director, Physical Sciences will be a senior member of the team reporting to the Senior Director of Licensing to set the strategic direction of the commercialization strategies for the University. He/she must be an energetic and experienced mid-career professional with an established record and experience, a solid deal sheet that demonstrates out-licensing deals done by the candidate, someone who is accessible, responsive, and fosters collaboration in a dynamic organizational culture to facilitate the translation of science and research to market. This position requires U.S. Citizenship due to access to Controlled Classified Information. Manager of Stamford Admissions and Recruitment Stamford Campus 499786 UConn Stamford Sep 18 2026 The UConn Stamford Campus seeks candidates for the position of Manager of Stamford Admissions and Recruitment (Senior Student Services Program Administrator). Reporting to the Campus Dean, the Manager of Stamford Admissions and Recruitment provides strategic leadership for undergraduate admissions, recruitment, and enrollment management initiatives for the Stamford campus. Executive Assistant, Governmental Relations (University Education Assistant 3) Government Relations 499804 UConn Storrs Sep 08 2026 The University of Connecticut’s Office of Governmental Relations is hiring an Executive Assistant in Storrs, CT. This position provides office management and