      "title": "UConn Cookie Information",
      "description": "UConn Careers | UConn Careers | University of Connecticut Skip to Navigation Skip to UConn Search Skip to Content Our websites may use cookies to personalize and enhance your experience. By continuing without changing your cookie settings, you agree to this collection. For more information, please see our University Websites Privacy Notice . UConn Cookie Information What are Cookies? Authentication Cookies Analytics Cookies Opt Out Web cookies (also called HTTP cookies , browser cookies , or simply cookies ) are small pieces of data that websites store on your device (computer, phone, etc.) through your web browser. They are used to remember information about you and your interactions with the site. Purpose of Cookies: Session Management : Keeping you logged in Remembering items in a shopping cart Saving language or theme preferences Personalization : Tailoring content or ads based on your previous activity Tracking & Analytics : Monitoring browsing behavior for analytics or marketing purposes Types of Cookies: Session Cookies : Temporary; deleted when you close your browser Used for things like keeping you logged in during a single session Persistent Cookies : Stored on your device until they expire or are manually deleted Used for remembering login credentials, settings, etc. First-Party Cookies : Set by the website you're visiting directly Third-Party Cookies : Set by other domains (usually advertisers) embedded in the website Commonly used for tracking across multiple sites Authentication cookies are a special type of web cookie used to identify and verify a user after they log in to a website or web application. What They Do: Once you log in to a site, the server creates an authentication cookie and sends it to your browser. This cookie: Proves to the website that you're logged in Prevents you from having to log in again on every page you visit Can persist across sessions if you select \"Remember me\" What's Inside an Authentication Cookie? Typically, it contains: A unique session ID (not your actual password) Optional metadata (e.g., expiration time, security flags) Analytics cookies are cookies used to collect data about how visitors interact with a website . Their primary purpose is to help website owners understand and improve user experience by analyzing things like: How users navigate the site Which pages are most/least visited How long users stay on each page What device, browser, or location the user is from What They Track: Some examples of data analytics cookies may collect: Page views and time spent on pages Click paths (how users move from page to page) Bounce rate (users who leave without interacting) User demographics (location, language, device) Referring websites (how users arrived at the site) Here’s how you can disable cookies in common browsers: 1. Google Chrome Open Chrome and click the three vertical dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies and other site data . Choose your preferred option: Block all cookies (not recommended, can break most websites). Block third-party cookies (can block ads and tracking cookies). 2. Mozilla Firefox Open Firefox and click the three horizontal lines in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy & Security . Under the Enhanced Tracking Protection section, choose Strict to block most cookies or Custom to manually choose which cookies to block. 3. Safari Open Safari and click Safari in the top-left corner of the screen. Go to Preferences > Privacy . Check Block all cookies to stop all cookies, or select options to block third-party cookies. 4. Microsoft Edge Open Edge and click the three horizontal dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy, search, and services > Cookies and site permissions . Select your cookie settings from there, including blocking all cookies or blocking third-party cookies. 5. On Mobile (iOS/Android) For Safari on iOS: Go to Settings > Safari > Privacy & Security > Block All Cookies . For Chrome on Android: Open the app, tap the three dots, go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies . Be Aware: Disabling cookies can make your online experience more difficult. Some websites may not load properly, or you may be logged out frequently. Also, certain features may not work as expected. UConn University of Connecticut Search University of Connecticut Search UConn A to Z Index UConn A to Z Index Site A-Z UConn A-Z UConn Careers Search this Site Search in https://wp.newemployees.hr.uconn.edu/> Search UConn Careers Apply for Jobs Applicant Login Career Portal Help Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine Your Search Filter Results Job mail subscription You can create a job alert and we will send you an e-mail when a position becomes available that matches your search criteria. To edit your job alert details please re-enter your search criteria, this will automatically override your previous subscription. Email address Keywords Keywords Work type Select All Full-time Part-time Categories Select All Academic Programs and Services Administrative Services Art, Museum and Theater Athletics (Coaches, Trainers, Specialists) Audit and Compliance Clerical Custodial Dining Services Executive Facilities Faculty Department Head/Director Faculty Extension Educator Faculty Lecturer Faculty Non Tenure Track Faculty Temporary Faculty Tenure Track Fiscal, Accounting and Budget Grants and Contracts Health and Safety Human Resources Information Technology Laboratory and Research Operations Legal Libraries Maintenance and Trades Marketing and Communication Postdoctoral Research Associates Public Safety Research Special Payroll Student Programs and Services Department Select All Academic Affairs Business Svcs Academic Interdisciplinary Academic Interdisciplinary (CETL) Academic Interdisciplinary (Enrichment Programs) Academic Operations Agriculture, Health, Natural Resources Agriculture,Health,Natural Rcs Agriculture,Health,Natural Rcs (CAHNR Acad Prog) Agriculture,Health,Natural Rcs (CAHNR Research) Agriculture,Health,Natural Rcs (Cooperative Extension System) Athletics Athletics Compliance Office Audit and Mgmt Advisory Svcs Avery Point Campus Budget and Planning Business Business (Business Faculty and Research) Business (Business Graduate Programs) Business (Business Undergrad Programs) CAHNR Chief Financial Officer CLAS Diversity and Inclusion Education Engineering Facilities Svcs and Univ Plan Facilities Svcs and Univ Plan (Facilities Operations) Facilities Svcs and Univ Plan (Planning, Design and Construct) Financial Oper and Controller Fine Arts Fine Arts (Fine Arts Institutes) General Counsel Global Affairs Government Relations Graduate Education Hartford Campus HR & Organizational Dev Inclusion and Civil Rights Ofc Information Technology Services Information Technology Svcs Institutional Equity Law Law School Liberal Arts and Sciences Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Administration) Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Humanities) Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Life and Behavioral Sci) Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Physical Sciences) Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS Social Sciences) Liberal Arts and Sciences (Collaborative Programs) Nursing Ombudsman Pharmacy President Procurement Procurement Services Provost Academic Affairs Provost Commitments Provost Misc Provost Office School of Engineering Social Work Stamford Campus Student Life and Enrollment Student Life and Enrollment (AVP of Student Life) Student Life and Enrollment (Career Readiness Life Skills) Student Life and Enrollment (Cultural Centers) Student Life and Enrollment (Dean of Students) Student Life and Enrollment (Student Affairs Administration) Student Success Student Success (Institute for Student Success) Student Success (Veteran Military Prog and Svcs) UConn Board of Trustees UConn Library UConn Library (Library Administration) UCONN Unit University Communications University Communications (Alumni Relations) University Compliance University Safety University Senate Vice President for Research Vice President for Research (Research Development) Vice President for Research (Research Integrity) Vice President for Research (Research Resources) Vice President for Research (Research Security) Vice President for Research (SPS Adminstration) Vice President for Research (Tech Comm and Industry Rltns) Waterbury Campus Back to jobs listing Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Powered by PageUp © University of Connecticut Disclaimers, Privacy & Copyright Accessibility Webmaster Login"
    },
    "https://jobs.hr.uconn.edu/cw/en-us/listing/": {
