      "title": "UConn Cookie Information",
      "description": "UConn Careers | UConn Careers | University of Connecticut Skip to Navigation Skip to UConn Search Skip to Content Our websites may use cookies to personalize and enhance your experience. By continuing without changing your cookie settings, you agree to this collection. For more information, please see our University Websites Privacy Notice . UConn Cookie Information What are Cookies? Authentication Cookies Analytics Cookies Opt Out Web cookies (also called HTTP cookies , browser cookies , or simply cookies ) are small pieces of data that websites store on your device (computer, phone, etc.) through your web browser. They are used to remember information about you and your interactions with the site. Purpose of Cookies: Session Management : Keeping you logged in Remembering items in a shopping cart Saving language or theme preferences Personalization : Tailoring content or ads based on your previous activity Tracking & Analytics : Monitoring browsing behavior for analytics or marketing purposes Types of Cookies: Session Cookies : Temporary; deleted when you close your browser Used for things like keeping you logged in during a single session Persistent Cookies : Stored on your device until they expire or are manually deleted Used for remembering login credentials, settings, etc. First-Party Cookies : Set by the website you're visiting directly Third-Party Cookies : Set by other domains (usually advertisers) embedded in the website Commonly used for tracking across multiple sites Authentication cookies are a special type of web cookie used to identify and verify a user after they log in to a website or web application. What They Do: Once you log in to a site, the server creates an authentication cookie and sends it to your browser. This cookie: Proves to the website that you're logged in Prevents you from having to log in again on every page you visit Can persist across sessions if you select \"Remember me\" What's Inside an Authentication Cookie? Typically, it contains: A unique session ID (not your actual password) Optional metadata (e.g., expiration time, security flags) Analytics cookies are cookies used to collect data about how visitors interact with a website . Their primary purpose is to help website owners understand and improve user experience by analyzing things like: How users navigate the site Which pages are most/least visited How long users stay on each page What device, browser, or location the user is from What They Track: Some examples of data analytics cookies may collect: Page views and time spent on pages Click paths (how users move from page to page) Bounce rate (users who leave without interacting) User demographics (location, language, device) Referring websites (how users arrived at the site) Here’s how you can disable cookies in common browsers: 1. Google Chrome Open Chrome and click the three vertical dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies and other site data . Choose your preferred option: Block all cookies (not recommended, can break most websites). Block third-party cookies (can block ads and tracking cookies). 2. Mozilla Firefox Open Firefox and click the three horizontal lines in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy & Security . Under the Enhanced Tracking Protection section, choose Strict to block most cookies or Custom to manually choose which cookies to block. 3. Safari Open Safari and click Safari in the top-left corner of the screen. Go to Preferences > Privacy . Check Block all cookies to stop all cookies, or select options to block third-party cookies. 4. Microsoft Edge Open Edge and click the three horizontal dots in the top-right corner. Go to Settings > Privacy, search, and services > Cookies and site permissions . Select your cookie settings from there, including blocking all cookies or blocking third-party cookies. 5. On Mobile (iOS/Android) For Safari on iOS: Go to Settings > Safari > Privacy & Security > Block All Cookies . For Chrome on Android: Open the app, tap the three dots, go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies . Be Aware: Disabling cookies can make your online experience more difficult. Some websites may not load properly, or you may be logged out frequently. Also, certain features may not work as expected. UConn University of Connecticut Search University of Connecticut Search UConn A to Z Index UConn A to Z Index Site A-Z UConn A-Z UConn Careers Search this Site Search in https://wp.newemployees.hr.uconn.edu/> Search UConn Careers Apply for Jobs Applicant Login Career Portal Help Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine Your Search Filter Results Work type Full-time 1 Locations UConn Storrs 1 Categories Information Technology 1 IT Manager Apply now Search #: 499714 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Information Technology JOB SUMMARY The University of Connecticut Information Technology Services (ITS) is seeking a Manager of Network Engineering and Operations to lead the University's Network Engineering and Network Operations teams. This position is responsible for overseeing the daily operation, support, and continuous improvement of the University's enterprise network infrastructure and services that support the academic, research, administrative, and residential communities across the Storrs campus, regional campuses, and the School of Law. Reporting to the Director of Network Services, the Manager provides leadership and operational oversight for network engineering, network operations, monitoring and management systems, automation initiatives, and related enterprise network services. The position is responsible for ensuring the availability, performance, security, and resiliency of mission-critical network services through effective staff leadership, operational management, process improvement, and technical governance. The Manager actively performs technology planning, service development, and network modernization initiatives while ensuring successful execution of departmental priorities and objectives. The successful candidate will be an experienced technical manager who can effectively balance operational leadership, personnel development, customer engagement, and technical oversight in a complex enterprise environment. The Manager fosters a culture of collaboration, accountability, continuous improvement, and service excellence while empowering staff to develop professionally and deliver reliable, high-quality services to the University community. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Foster a culture of collaboration, accountability, curiosity, innovation, continuous improvement, and exceptional customer service through leadership, mentoring and coaching. Provide unified leadership for the Network Engineering and Network Operations functional areas, ensuring coordinated planning, implementation, operation, observability and lifecycle management of enterprise network services. Provide management oversight for enterprise routing, switching, wireless networking, automation efforts, monitoring and management systems, DDI infrastructure, data center networks, and cloud connectivity. Empower technical staff to pursue professional development, acquire and apply new skills to automate systems and processes, improve efficiency and reduce toil. Serve as the primary management contact for customer communications, operational issues, service escalations and cross-functional coordination. Develop technology road maps, service strategies, methods and procedures, workforce plans in collaboration with the Director of Network Services to advance the network environment. Establish service objectives and metrics mapped to customer expectations for each target community and implement methods of observability to inform changes for continual improvement. Develop and implement integrated workflows with the Network Infrastructure, Data Center Operations and Telecommunications groups within Network Services and Information Security Engineering that result in a streamlined and accelerated deployment of network infrastructure, systems and services. Collaborate with peers and stakeholders to define and plan network services to meet University community and departmental objectives for IT system resiliency, business continuity, disaster recovery, information security and daily performance objectives. Promote team awareness and compliance with university policies, information security standards and applicable federal and state regulations. Define and manage change management procedures consistent with university and departmental policies and practices to ensure high availability and resiliency of network services. Oversee and develop departmental operating and project budget requests, manage funding and resources mapped to established priorities and monitor to ensure timely completion. Perform related duties as required. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Bachelor's degree and six (6) years of relevant experience; Associate degree and eight (8) years of relevant experience; or ten (10) years of progressively responsible experience in enterprise networking. Demonstrated experience leading technical teams, managing complex network infrastructure projects, mentoring technical staff, and supervising personnel, including a minimum of two (2) years of supervisory experience. Demonstrated experience administering enterprise technologies in mission-critical environments. Demonstrated knowledge of enterprise technologies with sufficient depth to mentor and coach technical staff in problem definition, decision making, planning, and communication. Demonstrated written and verbal communication skills with the ability to communicate effectively with engineers, executive leadership, vendors, and organizational stakeholders. Demonstrated knowledge of enterprise network services and platforms, including wired and wireless networking, firewall technologies, authentication and identity services, SIEM, IPAM, DNS, DHCP, network monitoring, and automation sufficient to provide effective technical oversight and critically evaluate technical recommendations, risks and proposed solutions. Demonstrated ability to balance strategic technology planning with hands-on engineering leadership, including budgeting, vendor management, project delivery, and operational service excellence. Experience managing and supporting 24x7 mission-critical network infrastructure, services and operational support processes. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience supporting higher education, research, healthcare, government, or other large multi-site enterprise organizations. Demonstrated experience of architecting, designing, implementing, and operating large-scale enterprise network environments, including campus LAN, WAN, wireless, cloud, and data center architectures. Experience administering enterprise network environments utilizing technologies comparable to Cisco Catalyst/Nexus, Juniper MX/QFX, HPE Mist/Aruba, Palo Alto, Fortinet, Cisco ISE, Infoblox, and Microsoft Azure networking solutions. Experience leveraging BGP, OSPF, MPLS, EVPN/VXLAN, traffic engineering, and software-defined networking technologies in complex enterprise environments. Experience developing network architecture standards, technology roadmaps, operational procedures, service delivery metrics, and continuous improvement initiatives. Professional certifications such as Cisco CCNP/CCIE, Juniper JNCIP/JNCIE, Palo Alto PCNSE, Aruba ACP/ACMP, ITSM/ITIL, PMP or equivalent industry credentials are desirable but not required. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, permanent position located at the Storrs Campus in Storrs, CT. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. This position is on-site.  This is not a remote position.  The position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule under applicable bargaining agreements and management approval.  We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #499714 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on September 14, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Sep 04 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Sep 18 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Department Search # Location Closes IT Manager Network Engr and Design 499714 UConn Storrs Sep 18 2026 The University of Connecticut Information Technology Services (ITS) is seeking a Manager of Network Engineering and Operations to lead the University's Network Engineering and Network Operations teams. This position is responsible for overseeing the daily operation, support, and continuous improvement of the University's enterprise network infrastructure and services that support the academic, research, administrative, and residential communities across the Storrs campus, regional campuses, and the School of Law. Current opportunities Position Department Search # Location Closes IT Manager Network Engr and Design 499714 UConn Storrs Sep 18 2026 The University of Connecticut Information Technology Services (ITS) is seeking a Manager of Network Engineering and Operations to lead the University's Network Engineering and Network Operations teams. This position is responsible for overseeing the daily operation, support, and continuous improvement of the University's enterprise network infrastructure and services that support the academic, research, administrative, and residential communities across the Storrs campus, regional campuses, and the School of Law. Powered by PageUp © University of Connecticut Disclaimers, Privacy & Copyright Accessibility Webmaster Login"
