and services > Cookies and site permissions . Select your cookie settings from there, including blocking all cookies or blocking third-party cookies. 5. On Mobile (iOS/Android) For Safari on iOS: Go to Settings > Safari > Privacy & Security > Block All Cookies . For Chrome on Android: Open the app, tap the three dots, go to Settings > Privacy and security > Cookies . Be Aware: Disabling cookies can make your online experience more difficult. Some websites may not load properly, or you may be logged out frequently. Also, certain features may not work as expected. UConn University of Connecticut Search University of Connecticut Search UConn A to Z Index UConn A to Z Index Site A-Z UConn A-Z UConn Careers Search this Site Search in https://wp.newemployees.hr.uconn.edu/> Search UConn Careers Apply for Jobs Applicant Login Career Portal Help Subscribe to Job Alerts Refine Your Search Filter Results Work type Full-time 1 Locations UConn Storrs 1 Categories Information Technology 1 Network Service Administrator 1 or 2 Apply now Search #: 499730 Work type: Full-time Location: UConn Storrs Categories: Information Technology JOB SUMMARY Under the supervision of a designated team leader, the Network Administrator 1/2 for Collaboration Services provides technical support for the planning, implementation, administration, monitoring, troubleshooting, and lifecycle management of the University's enterprise voice and collaboration services and supporting network infrastructure. The position supports the integration of voice and collaboration platforms with network, identity, telecommunications carrier, and other enterprise systems and participates in the evaluation and implementation of technology solutions. Click here for additional information about the University. Click here for detailed position information and the job description. DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES Supports enterprise voice, collaboration, and associated network services, including installation, provisioning, configuration, monitoring, upgrading, troubleshooting, and decommissioning of systems and endpoints. Performs needs analysis for voice and collaboration services with end users, technical staff, and stakeholders. Provides production support and daily administration of systems, applications, and infrastructure used to deliver voice and collaboration services. Works with senior technical staff and colleagues to plan and implement system integrations, technology changes, and problem resolution. Identifies and resolves system problems and service degradations using appropriate diagnostic and monitoring tools, including investigation of network and call-quality issues. Deploys, configures, and supports hardware and software used to deliver and manage enterprise voice and collaboration services. Participates in the development of technical requirements, implementation plans, testing procedures, and procurement documentation. Collaborate with technical peers, telecommunications carriers, vendors, service providers, and manufacturer technical support resources as necessary to implement and support services. Develops and maintains system documentation, operating procedures, knowledge base materials, and end-user documentation. Supports automation of service provisioning, administration, and decommissioning and responds to emergency network, voice, or collaboration service outages. Performs related work as required. ADDITIONAL DUTIES AND RESPONSIBILITIES FOR NETWORK ADMINISTRATOR 2 Analyzes complex technical and service requirements and recommends voice, collaboration, and supporting network technology solutions. Defines technical and project requirements and develops specifications, statements of work, implementation plans, and testing and acceptance procedures. Independently diagnoses and resolves complex system, integration, interoperability, and service-quality problems. Plans and implements integrations between voice and collaboration platforms and related network, identity, carrier, and enterprise systems. Develops and implements automation, monitoring, and management methods to improve service provisioning, operational efficiency, performance, and reliability. Leads larger technical assignments and coordinates vendors, carriers, service providers, and cross-functional technical resources to implement and maintain highly available voice and collaboration services. MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS Associate's degree and four years of related experience; OR Bachelor's degree and two years of related experience; OR Six years of related experience. Experience supporting voice, collaboration, telecommunications, or related network services in an enterprise environment. Demonstrated knowledge of networking concepts and technologies supporting IP-based voice and collaboration services. Demonstrated knowledge of scripting or automation tools. Effective written and oral communication, troubleshooting, and problem-solving skills. Ability to work effectively in a team environment and with technical and non-technical users. Ability to travel to university locations and work outside normal business hours when necessary to support service maintenance or restoration. ADDITIONAL MINIMUM QUALIFICATIONS FOR APPOINTMENT AS NETWORK ADMINISTRATOR 2 Associate's degree and six years of related experience; OR Bachelor's degree and four years of related experience; OR Eight years of related experience. Demonstrated experience configuring, administering, and troubleshooting enterprise VoIP and collaboration systems and services. Demonstrated experience independently diagnosing and resolving complex technical problems involving voice, collaboration, and supporting network technologies. Demonstrated experience with enterprise Cisco collaboration and Unified Communications systems and endpoints. PREFERRED QUALIFICATIONS Experience planning, implementing, administering, and supporting enterprise VoIP and collaboration platforms, including Cisco Unified Communications Manager (CUCM)/WebEx and/or Microsoft Teams Voice. Knowledge of VoIP protocols, standards, call routing, and network technologies supporting real-time communications, including SIP, QoS, routing, switching, firewalls, IP addressing, and virtualization. Experience administering and troubleshooting contact center technologies, including call queues, routing, and related scripting or workflows. Experience working with telecommunications carriers and service providers to provision, integrate, and manage SIP, VoIP, and traditional telecommunications services. Experience with monitoring and diagnostic tools used to evaluate system availability, network performance, and voice/call quality. Experience planning or supporting highly available telecommunications systems in accordance with applicable regulatory requirements, information security practices, and industry standards. Experience integrating voice and collaboration platforms with enterprise identity and access management systems such as Microsoft Entra ID and Active Directory, including automated provisioning and deprovisioning and identity lifecycle management. Experience developing scripts, APIs, or other automation methods for provisioning, administration, monitoring, or lifecycle management of enterprise services. APPOINTMENT TERMS This is a full-time, on-site, permanent position. The position may be eligible for a hybrid work schedule under applicable bargaining agreements and management approval.  We are unable to provide visa sponsorship for this position. The University offers a competitive salary, and outstanding benefits , including employee and dependent tuition waivers at UConn, and a highly desirable work environment. Classification and salary will be commensurate with successful candidates’ background and experience. Other rights, terms, and conditions of employment are contained in the collective bargaining agreement between the University of Connecticut and the University of Connecticut Professional Employees Association (UCPEA). TERMS AND CONDITIONS OF EMPLOYMENT Employment of the successful candidate is contingent upon the successful completion of a pre-employment criminal background check. TO APPLY Please apply online at Faculty and Staff Positions , Search #496730 to upload a resume , cover letter , and contact information for three (3) professional references . Applicants must clearly demonstrate how they meet the stated minimum qualifications, and any preferred qualifications they may possess, in their application materials. This job posting is scheduled to be removed at 11:55 p.m. Eastern time on September 11, 2026. All employees are subject to adherence to the State Code of Ethics . All members of the University of Connecticut are expected to exhibit appreciation of, and contribute to, an inclusive, respectful, and diverse environment for the University community. The University of Connecticut aspires to create a community built on collaboration and belonging and has actively sought to create an inclusive culture within the workforce. The success of the University is dependent on the willingness of our diverse employee and student populations to share their rich perspectives and backgrounds in a respectful manner. This makes it essential for each member of our community to feel secure and welcomed and to thoroughly understand and believe that their ideas are respected by all. We strongly respect each individual employee’s unique experiences and perspectives and encourage all members of the community to do the same. All applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, ethnicity, religion, age, sex, marital status, national origin, ancestry, sexual orientation, genetic information, physical or mental disabilities, veteran’s status, status as a victim of domestic violence and/or sexual assault and/or trafficking in persons as defined by Connecticut law, prior conviction of a crime, workplace hazards to the reproductive systems, or gender identity or expression . The University of Connecticut is an AA/EEO employer including for Disability and Veteran status. Advertised: Aug 27 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Applications close: Sep 11 2026 Eastern Daylight Time Back to search results Apply now Refer a friend Whatsapp Facebook LinkedIn Email App Send me jobs like these We will email you new jobs that match this search. Ok, we will send you jobs like this. The email address was invalid, please check for errors. You must agree to the privacy statement Subscribe Recaptcha Privacy agreement Search results Position Department Search # Location Closes Network Service Administrator 1 or 2 Telecommunications 499730 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 Under the supervision of a designated team leader, the Network Administrator 1/2 for Collaboration Services provides technical support for the planning, implementation, administration, monitoring, troubleshooting, and lifecycle management of the University's enterprise voice and collaboration services and supporting network infrastructure. The position supports the integration of voice and collaboration platforms with network, identity, telecommunications carrier, and other enterprise systems and participates in the evaluation and implementation of technology solutions. Current opportunities Position Department Search # Location Closes Network Service Administrator 1 or 2 Telecommunications 499730 UConn Storrs Sep 11 2026 Under the supervision of a designated team leader, the Network Administrator 1/2 for Collaboration Services provides technical support for the planning, implementation, administration, monitoring, troubleshooting, and lifecycle management of the University's enterprise voice and collaboration services and supporting network infrastructure. The position supports the integration of voice and collaboration platforms with network, identity, telecommunications carrier, and other enterprise systems and participates in the evaluation and implementation of technology solutions. Powered by PageUp © University of Connecticut Disclaimers, Privacy & Copyright Accessibility Webmaster Login"
