 Location Closes Visiting Assistant Extension Educator in Land Use Dept of Extension Middlesex (Department of Extension) 499671 Middlesex County Extension Ctr Sep 25 2026 We seek an individual whose professional skills and abilities can provide statewide outreach and training to land use commissioners and others on issues related to land use planning and decision making. This position will lead the award-winning Land Use Academy in the  Center for Land Use Education and Research, advance the Center’s mission of supporting communities in balancing growth and natural resource protection, and have the opportunity to contribute to efforts to connect undergraduates with community extension work. Assistant/Associate/Full Professor Nursing Instruct and Research 499521 UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut, Elisabeth DeLuca School of Nursing is seeking applications to fill a full-time, 9-month, tenure-track/tenured Assistant/Associate/Full Professor position. Candidates with research expertise in the following areas are encouraged to apply: health equity across the lifespan; social determinants of health; parent-child health: support for people with acute and chronic conditions, including symptoms and self-management; and biobehavioral studies of sleep and pain. UConn Regional Campus Nurse Navigator (RN) - 9-month - Stamford Campus Student Health and Wellness 499587 UConn Stamford UConn Student Health and Wellness is searching for a 9-month Nurse Navigator (RN) to provide professional nursing and health services to the Stamford Regional Campus. As a college health nurse, this registered nurse will be responsible for providing patient focused advice and education, by supporting the maintenance and improvement of the health of students, identifying, and assisting in removing or modifying health related barriers, and supporting early detection and early intervention strategies. Assistant/Associate Professor of Business Law Marketing 499584 UConn Storrs The University of Connecticut, School of Business, is seeking applications to fill a full-time, 9-month, tenure/tenure track Assistant/Associate Professor position in Business Law. Candidates with a broad range of relevant curricular and scholarly expertise are encouraged to apply, with a particular emphasis on research and teaching interests in business law. We especially welcome applications from candidates whose experience, scholarship, or perspectives would contribute to the diversity and inclusiveness of our faculty and academic community. Custodian - Various Work Schedules/Multiple Buildings - (Two Positions) FO Custodial Services 499544 UConn Storrs Sep 30 2026 The Facilities Operations Department has two job openings for permanent, full-time custodian positions. The work schedule for these positions may be either 1st Shift Wednesday – Sunday, 7:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m., OR 1st Shift Saturday – Wednesday, 7:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m. dependent upon operating needs.  These positions are open to the public. Instructor in Residence - Stamford Chemistry 499530 UConn Stamford The Chemistry Department within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) at the University of Connecticut, Stamford, invites applications for an Instructor in Residence (IiR) position. The successful candidate will primarily be responsible for teaching general chemistry laboratory and organic chemistry laboratory sections in collaboration with other full-time faculty members. Maintenance Supervisor 1 - General (Stamford Campus) - 1 Position FO Regional Campus Service (FO Operations Services) 498586 UConn Stamford Sep 30 2026 UConn’s Facilities Operations Department has a job opening for a Maintenance Supervisor 1 – General position at the Stamford Campus. This is a permanent, full-time, 1st shift position, with a work schedule of Monday – Friday, 8:00 a.m. to 4:00 p.m., 37.5 hours per week with an unpaid half an hour for lunch. Qualified Craft Worker (Plumbing and Steamfitting), Multiple Positions/Various Work Schedules (Four Positions) FO Mechanical and Plumbng Svcs (FO Trade Services) (FO Energy and Trade Services) 499014 UConn Storrs Sep 30 2026 The State of Connecticut, University of Connecticut’s Facilities Operations Department has  four job openings for Qualified Craft Worker (QCW) – Plumbing positions at the Storrs Campus.  These are permanent, full-time, 37.5 hours/week positions with a variety of work schedules. Water Pollution Control Operator 1, 40 Hour Work Week, Work Schedule TBD Dependent on Operating Needs: 1st Shift Sunday - Thursday OR 1st Shift Tuesday - Saturday; 1 Position FO Conservation and Compliance (FO Energy and Trade Services) 499413 UConn Storrs Sep 30 2026 Seeking a Water Pollution Control Operator 1 to work at UConn Facilities Operations Class IV, Water Resource Recovery Facility (WRRF) to include water reclamation and associated lift stations to the facility. This is a full-time, permanent position. The work schedule is to be determined based on operating needs; the work schedule will be either 1st Shift Sunday – Thursday OR 1st Shift Tuesday – Saturday. The work hours will be 7:00 a.m. to 3:00 p.m. with a paid half an hour for lunch. This position is categorized as “Open to the Public”. Residence Hall Director Residential Life 499384 UConn Storrs UConn's Residential Life team is seeking dedicated, student-focused applicants for Residence Hall Director (HD) positions. In this live-in, full-time position, you'll play a pivotal role in fostering a safe, inclusive, and engaging residential community for 400-700 residents. This dynamic position combines student learning and growth, community development, and supervision within one of New England's top public universities. Police Officer Trainee Police Department 499338 UConn Storrs Dec 01 2026 Are you ready for an exciting and rewarding career? Join the University of Connecticut Police Department, an internationally accredited agency, and help protect Connecticut’s future while serving a diverse and dynamic community. With competitive salaries ranging from $49,849 to $64,489 depending on state service (plus $5,000 in additional stipends) and a comprehensive benefits package, this is your chance to make a real impact. Apply now to become part of a team that offers diverse challenges, including community engagement, law enforcement, and the opportunity to work across multiple UConn campuses statewide! Storrs Police Officer (Certified) Police Department 499343 UConn Storrs Dec 01 2026 Are you ready for an exciting and rewarding career? Join the University of Connecticut Police Department, an internationally accredited agency, and help protect Connecticut’s future while serving a diverse and dynamic community. With competitive salaries ranging from $67,519 to $84,153 depending on state service (plus $5,000 in additional stipends) and a comprehensive benefits package, this is your chance to make a real impact. Apply now to become part of a team that offers diverse challenges, including community engagement, law enforcement, and the opportunity to work at the Storrs location Stamford Police Officer (Certified) Police Department 499333 UConn Stamford Dec 01 2026 Are you ready for an exciting and rewarding career? Join the University of Connecticut Police Department, an internationally accredited agency, and help protect Connecticut’s future while serving a diverse and dynamic community. With competitive salaries ranging from $67,519 to $84,153 depending on state service (plus $5,000 in additional stipends) and a comprehensive benefits package, this is your chance to make a real impact. Apply now to become part of a team that offers diverse challenges, including community engagement, law enforcement, and the opportunity to work in Stamford location UCH Police Officer (Certified) Police Department 499334 UConn Health (Farmington) Dec 01 2026 Are you ready for an exciting and rewarding career? Join the University of Connecticut Police Department, an internationally accredited agency, and help protect Connecticut’s future while serving a diverse and dynamic community. With competitive salaries ranging from $67,519 to $84,153 depending on state service (plus $5,000 in additional stipends) and a comprehensive benefits package, this is your chance to make a real impact. Apply now to become part of a team that offers diverse challenges, including community engagement, law enforcement, and the opportunity to work in Farmington location Department Head Plant Science and Landscape Architecture Plant Sci and Landscape Arch 499238 UConn Storrs The Department of Plant Science and Landscape Architecture within the College of Agriculture, Health and Natural Resources, at the University of Connecticut (UConn) invites applications for the position of Department Head with an appointment at the rank of Professor or Associate Professor. We seek an inspirational, dynamic, and visionary individual to provide strong academic and administrative leadership for a highly ranked and productive department, in alignment with the strategic plans for the College and the University. Postdoctoral Research Associate Electrical and Computer Engr 499299 UConn Storrs The Physiological Acoustics Lab (http://escabilab.uconn.edu) at the University of Connecticut seeks applicants for a postdoctoral position in systems and computational neuroscience. Instructor in Residence Chemistry 499127 UConn Storrs The Chemistry Department within the College of Liberal Arts and Sciences (CLAS) at the University of Connecticut invites applications for an Instructor in Residence (IiR) position. The successful candidate will primarily be responsible for teaching general chemistry laboratory and organic chemistry laboratory sections. Assistant/Associate Extension Educator for Agriculture Business Management Department of Extension 497670 Other - please see posting for additional information This is a full-time, 11-month appointment for a non-tenure-track position at the rank of Assistant/Associate Extension Educator. The successful candidate is expected to develop strong working relationships with producers throughout the state; interact with UConn faculty, state, and federal agency personnel; and develop interdisciplinary extension programs. Water Pollution Control Operator 2, 40 Hour Work Week, 1st Shift Tuesday – Saturday, 7:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m. OR 1st Shift Sunday – Thursday, 7:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m. (1 position) FO Conservation and Compliance (FO Energy and Trade Services) 498644 UConn Storrs Sep 30 2026 UConn’s Facilities Operations Department has a job opening for a Water Pollution Control Operator 2 position at the Water Resource Recovery Facility located at the Storrs Campus. This is a permanent, full-time position, with a work schedule of 1st Shift Tuesday – Saturday, 7:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m. OR 1st Shift Sunday – Thursday, 7:00 a.m. – 3:00 p.m., 40 hours per week with a paid half an hour for lunch.  The work schedule is to be determined and will be based on operating needs. Electronic Integrated Control Systems Tech (Building Subsystems) One 2nd Shift M-F Position FO Conservation and Compliance (FO Energy and Trade Services) 497487 UConn Storrs Sep 30 2026 The Facilities Operations Department at the Storrs Campus has one 2nd Shift job opening for Electronic Integrated Control System Technician (Building Subsystems) position. This position is a permanent, full-time position; the work schedule for 2nd Shift positions is M-F, 3:00 p.m. to 11:00 p.m. QCW HVACR Multiple Positions/Various Work Schedules (4 Positions) FO Mechanical and Plumbng Svcs (FO Trade Services) (FO Energy and Trade Services) 497929 UConn Storrs Sep 30 2026 The State of Connecticut, University of Connecticut’s Facilities Operations Department has four current job openings for Qualified Craft Worker (QCW) – HVACR positions at the Storrs Campus. These are permanent, full-time, 37.5 hours/week positions with a variety of work schedules. Current opportunities Position Department Se